+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional `dueDate`; the API reports and filters `overdue`, the list page shows both and offers a „nur überfällige“ filter.
+
+**Architecture:** The store owns the rule: `createStore({ now })` validates `dueDate`, computes `overdue` on every output (returning copies), and filters in `list({ overdue })`. `app.mjs` only parses `?overdue=`. The page renders server fields and refetches with the API filter.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, `node:http`, `node:test`, plain HTML/JS. Zero dependencies.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-faelligkeitsdatum-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` → HTTP 400.
+- TDD: failing test in `test/` first.
+- `dueDate` is `"YYYY-MM-DD"` or `null`; overdue ⇔ `dueDate !== null && !done && dueDate < today(UTC)`.
+- „Heute“ = `now().toISOString().slice(0, 10)` (UTC).
+- New UI elements carry `data-testid`: `todo-due`, `todo-overdue`, `filter-overdue`. Copy: „überfällig“, „nur überfällige“.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. Completing an overdue todo (`PATCH {done:true}`) → response and list show `overdue: false` immediately. (Task 1)
+2. Time passing without any write → a todo due yesterday-relative-to-new-now becomes overdue (computed on read, not stored). (Task 1)
+3. Calendar edge cases: `2024-02-29` valid; `2026-02-29`, `2026-1-5`, `2026-13-01`, `20261005` rejected. (Task 1)
+4. A PATCH with one invalid field (`{title:'B', dueDate:'x'}`) → 400 and nothing changed (validate all before mutating). (Task 1)
+5. `?overdue=TRUE`, `?overdue=` or `?overdue=1` → 400, not silently ignored. (Task 2)
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store — `dueDate`, computed `overdue`, filtered `list`
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Create: `test/store.test.mjs`
+- Modify: `test/app.test.mjs` (existing `creates and lists todos` expectation)
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: `createStore({ now = () => new Date() } = {})`; every method returning todos returns copies shaped `{ id, title, done, dueDate, overdue }`; `list({ overdue } = {})` where `overdue` is `true | false | undefined` (undefined = all). `add({ title, dueDate })`, `update(id, patch)` accept `dueDate`; `overdue` key in `add` input or `patch` → `ValidationError`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests** in `test/store.test.mjs`, with `const now = () => new Date('2026-10-23T23:30:00Z')` (late UTC on the 23rd):
+  - `add` without `dueDate` → `{ id: 1, title: 'A', done: false, dueDate: null, overdue: false }`.
+  - `dueDate: '2026-10-22'` → `overdue: true`; `'2026-10-23'` → `false`; `'2026-10-24'` → `false`.
+  - done todo with `'2026-10-01'` → `overdue: false`; `update(id, { done: true })` on an overdue todo returns `overdue: false` (Review Focus 1).
+  - mutable clock: `let t = new Date('2026-10-23T12:00:00Z')`, store with `now: () => t`, add `'2026-10-23'` → `false`; set `t = new Date('2026-10-24T00:00:00Z')` → `get(1).overdue === true` (Review Focus 2).
+  - `update(id, { dueDate: null })` → `dueDate: null, overdue: false`.
+  - `assert.throws(..., ValidationError)` for `dueDate` values `'2026-02-29'`, `'2026-1-5'`, `'2026-13-01'`, `'20261005'`, `'morgen'`, `20261023`, `true`, in both `add` and `update`; `'2024-02-29'` accepted (Review Focus 3).
+  - `overdue: true` in `add` input or `update` patch throws `ValidationError`.
+  - `update(1, { title: 'B', dueDate: 'x' })` throws and `get(1).title === 'A'` (Review Focus 4).
+  - `list({ overdue: true })` / `list({ overdue: false })` / `list()` partition a set of past, today, none, done-past todos correctly (compare ids).
+  - mutating a returned object (`store.get(1).title = 'X'`) does not change `store.get(1).title`.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run** `node --test test/store.test.mjs` — Expected: FAIL (`dueDate` undefined etc.).
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** in `src/store.mjs`: a `parseDueDate(value)` helper (null/undefined → `null`; string matching `/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/` that round-trips through `new Date(value + 'T00:00:00Z').toISOString().slice(0, 10)`; else `ValidationError('dueDate must be a YYYY-MM-DD date or null')`); a `view(todo)` that returns `{ ...todo, overdue }`; in `update`, validate every present field before assigning any. Store keeps `{ id, title, done, dueDate }` internally.
+- [ ] **Step 4: Update** `test/app.test.mjs` `creates and lists todos` expectation to `[{ id: 1, title: 'Milch kaufen', done: false, dueDate: null, overdue: false }]`.
+- [ ] **Step 5: Run** `npm test` — Expected: all PASS.
+- [ ] **Step 6: Commit** `git add src/store.mjs test/ && git commit -m "feat: due dates and overdue in store (#1)"`
+
+### Task 2: API — `?overdue=` filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/app.mjs` (`GET /todos` branch)
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `createStore({ now })`, `store.list({ overdue })` from Task 1.
+- Produces: `GET /todos?overdue=true|false`; other values → 400 `{ error }`.
