+  - `?overdue=TRUE`, `?overdue=`, `?overdue=1` → 400 each (Review Focus 5).
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run** `node --test test/app.test.mjs` — Expected: filter tests FAIL (all 4 returned), 400 tests FAIL.
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** in `src/app.mjs`: if `url.searchParams.has('overdue')`, map `'true'`/`'false'` to booleans, otherwise throw `new ValidationError('overdue must be true or false')`; pass to `store.list({ overdue })`.
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run** `npm test` — Expected: all PASS.
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** `git add src/app.mjs test/app.test.mjs && git commit -m "feat: filter todos by overdue (#1)"`
+
+### Task 3: List page — due date, „überfällig“, „nur überfällige“
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `public/index.html`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs` (`serves the list page`)
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: todo fields `dueDate`, `overdue`; `GET /todos?overdue=true` from Task 2.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Extend** `serves the list page` to also `assert.match` the HTML against `/data-testid="filter-overdue"/` and `/nur überfällige/`.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run** `node --test test/app.test.mjs` — Expected: FAIL.
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** in `public/index.html`: `<label><input type="checkbox" data-testid="filter-overdue"> nur überfällige</label>` above the list; a `render()` that clears the list, fetches `/todos?overdue=true` when checked else `/todos`, and per item appends after the title a `span[data-testid=todo-due]` with `dueDate` (only if non-null) and a `span[data-testid=todo-overdue]` with `überfällig` (only if `overdue`), separated by spaces; `change` listener calls `render()`. No styling. Keep existing testids and „✓“.
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run** `npm test` — Expected: all PASS.
